{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 to rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily, retain seven compressed rotations, and preserve open writer file descriptors using copytruncate. Configuration and log data persisted across a verified node restart.","actions_performed":["Installed /etc/logrotate.d/inventory with daily, rotate 7, compress, missingok, notifempty, and copytruncate.","Validated the rule with logrotate debug parsing.","Forced an isolated rotation and verified compression plus continued writing through an already-open file descriptor.","Restarted node1 safely and confirmed its boot identity changed.","Verified crond, configuration, current log data, and compressed rotated data recovered after restart."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Rotate daily and retain seven compressed rotations","command_ids":["cmd-fcc12f86046a4cf3","cmd-978d93bb13ee47b6","cmd-7d9f3579cf9d49c4"],"summary":"The installed rule parses as daily with seven rotations; forced rotation created a valid gzip archive, and the policy remained valid after restart."},{"requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation","command_ids":["cmd-978d93bb13ee47b6"],"summary":"The active log retained inode 33575371 across forced rotation, and a write through the descriptor opened before rotation appeared in the current log afterward."},{"requirement":"node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-f0452e7fa1ca4145","cmd-3d168dabfd18403a","cmd-acba323864d44a4c","cmd-7d9f3579cf9d49c4"],"summary":"Pre-restart boot ID was a8e7c48c-f025-4f14-9fd0-ef6c37642e45; restart was acknowledged; post-restart boot ID changed to 9248faef-b48e-4b3c-b57b-92d960a8755c; crond, the rule, current data, and compressed archive all recovered."}]}
